\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Trace distance vs. fidelity distance computed with the JTC for the quantum-inspired nearest-mean classifier (QNM-C) using the inverse stereographic encoding. The $R^2$ value of $0.986$ indicates a strong linear relationship between the two measures, confirming that the JTC can effectively estimate the trace distance from the fidelity.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trace_vs_fidelity}{{8}{7}{Trace distance vs. fidelity distance computed with the JTC for the quantum-inspired nearest-mean classifier (QNM-C) using the inverse stereographic encoding. The $R^2$ value of $0.986$ indicates a strong linear relationship between the two measures, confirming that the JTC can effectively estimate the trace distance from the fidelity.\relax }{figure.caption.25}{}}
